   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CPC Partnership: Prevalence Study of Child Trafficking in Jamaica</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to support the Government of Jamaica (GOJ) to enhance its capacity to combat child trafficking in line with the Child Protection Compact (CPC) agreement between the US Government and the GOJ through research to assess the prevalence of child trafficking as well as risk factors, exploitation dynamics of child sex and labour trafficking in Jamaica. The research will be conducted by carrying out survey(s) to assess prevalence, risk factors, exploitation dynamics, and health and safety risks of child sex and labour trafficking. This research will provide the Government of Jamaica with data that will positively impact their ability to conduct victim-centered investigations, prosecutions, and convictions of child trafficking cases as well as to provide comprehensive assistance and increase efforts to prevent child trafficking.  The project will therefore contribute to Objective 3 of the CPC agreement, in particular through point 3.1 &#x201c;conduct nationwide research on the prevalence of child sex and labour trafficking in Jamaica&#x201d;.</narrative>
  </description>
